@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Harness image layers — venvs, what each image refuses to ship, and PATH order

' purpose: the per-harness build decisions that are not lineage, not version
'          pinning and not user identity — what goes in a venv, what is
'          deliberately absent, and the two places PATH and prefix order matter
' covers: defs/cecli/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/cursor/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/opencode/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/claudecode/solidity/Dockerfile
'
' Elsewhere on purpose:
'   which parent, which tag ....... _spec/_devops/image-lineage-and-publish.puml
'   why every agent is pinned ..... _spec/_devops/agent-version-pin.puml
'   /home/agent and the alias ..... _spec/_paradigms/runtime-user-boundary.puml
'   the harden pass ............... _spec/defs/harden-pass.puml
'   no docker binaries, and the
'   evidence against that call .... _spec/_plans/image-size-reduction.puml
'   the plugin seed ............... _spec/defs/claudecode/lsp-plugins-seed.puml
'   house rules as managed policy . _spec/packages/lib/house-rules.puml
'
' ── cecli: TWO VENVS, AND A BYTECODE PREFIX INSTEAD OF A SWITCH ─────────────
' cecli is the aider fork (cecli-dev) in a Python venv on proveo/base. No Node,
' no browsers — deduped from the old MCR playwright/python variant.
'
' PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=/tmp/proveo-pycache, NOT PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1. The
' full chain, because two of the three steps look wrong on their own:
'   * pip byte-compiles at INSTALL time regardless of PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE —
'     that variable is a RUNTIME switch. So both venvs shipped .py AND .pyc:
'     153 MB measured.
'   * `pip install --no-compile` removes them. But paired with
'     PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE the modules are then never regenerated either, so
'     every launch re-parses everything, forever: `cecli --version` measured
'     876 ms -> 1850 ms.
'   * So bytecode IS written, to a prefix OUTSIDE the read-only venv that any
'     run-as uid can create. Measured at uid 4242: first launch 2258 ms, then
'     711 ms — FASTER than the 876 ms baseline, because the cache holds only
'     what was actually imported. (The same pairing measured during the size
'     work reported 2315 ms then 679/712 ms; both runs agree on the shape.)
' /tmp is the right home for it: per-sandbox, world-writable, and nothing needs
' it to survive the sandbox.
'
' NO build-essential, AND THE VENVS STILL BUILD. It used to be installed
' permanently so pip could compile sdists. Measured: of cecli-dev's and
' serena-agent's ENTIRE dependency closures exactly ONE arrives as an sdist
' (proxy_tools 0.1.0) and it is pure Python, so setuptools alone builds its
' wheel. gcc-14, g++-14, cpp-14, binutils, libstdc++-dev, libgcc-dev and
' linux-libc-dev were ~190 MB shipped to an agent image for a compiler nothing
' invoked. Verified by building both venvs on a base with no compiler at all
' before the removal landed.
'
' SERENA GETS ITS OWN VENV. cecli has no native LSP client, so its code
' intelligence arrives as MCP — the same delivery cursor gets from
' mcp-language-server. serena-agent and cecli-dev disagree about dependency
' versions, so they cannot share a prefix; only the stdio launcher is symlinked
' onto PATH. It is pinned for the reason the layer was deleted the FIRST time: an
' unpinned `pip install serena-agent` shipped a version skew that left the server
' dead on every boot for weeks. packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' (configure_cecli_mcp) refuses to declare a server that will not answer an
' initialize handshake.
'
' apt here: python3, python3-pip, python3-venv, iptables, less.
' ENV: PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1, PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1, CECLI_HOME=/app/.cecli.
'
' ── iptables STAYS IN ALL FOUR, AND IT IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT ──────────────────
' iptables is the DAEMON's dependency, not the harness's: sbx's per-sandbox
' daemon builds its own NAT chain at start and cannot without it. It stays even
' though no image ships dockerd any more — a NAT chain needs iptables whoever
' builds it. The same reasoning keeps the `docker` group (`groupadd -f docker`
' plus `usermod -aG docker` for both the harness user and `agent`, because the
' socket is created root:docker) and the
' `com.docker.sandboxes.start-docker="true"` LABEL, which is what sbx reads to
' decide whether to start a daemon at all; without it sbx records `dind: false`
' at container creation and `docker version` answers "Cannot connect to the
' Docker daemon" beside Compose files the agent can plainly read.
'
' ── opencode: xclip IS ABSENT ON PURPOSE ────────────────────────────────────
' xclip needs an X display. This container has none and sets no DISPLAY, and the
' package drags libx11/libxmu/libxt/libxext along for a clipboard that cannot
' exist. Nothing in the tree ever invoked it. plantuml and plantuml-lsp arrive
' from proveo/base-node-lsp rather than being installed here, as do the shared
' workspace language servers — only the opencode agent itself is installed in
' this file.
'
' ── claudecode: THE DEV TOOLS EVERY REPO PINS ITSELF ARE ABSENT ─────────────
' No global typescript / ts-node / prettier / eslint. 65 MB measured, unpinned
' (so a warm cache could serve last year's), and a fifth copy of typescript in an
' image whose three LSP servers each bundle their own. The language SERVERS stay:
' they come from proveo/base-node-lsp and are what the LSP plugin seed keys on.
'
' The same argument is why NODE_ENV is deliberately NOT baked. Setting it to
' production would make every `npm`/`pnpm install` the agent runs in the
' workspace skip devDependencies — tsc, eslint, test runners — which are exactly
' the tools the agent needs. It is left undefined so the project's own .env can
' set it if it wants one (load_env exports .env with `set -a`).
'
' WORKSPACE ROOTS. /app is the workspace root, the same as every other def.
' /workspace survives only for the parts that were never claudecode's own:
' `--data-dir` mounts at /workspace/data for EVERY harness, so that path is a
' cross-harness convention rather than a leftover of the retired input-output
' layout. Modes as built: /workspace 755, /app 750, /workspace/data 750,
' /app/output 755, /workspace/temp 755, /workspace/mcp-servers 755.
'
' The sandbox theme is baked to /opt/proveo/themes and installed into the agent
' home by the seed, so it reaches BOTH backends rather than only docker.
'
' KNOWN DEFECT, recorded rather than fixed here: the HEALTHCHECK hard-codes
' /home/claude while USER_NAME is a build ARG, so any build with a different
' USER_NAME is permanently unhealthy.
'
' ── cursor: THE ENTERPRISE HOOK LAYER ───────────────────────────────────────
' /etc/cursor/hooks.json is copied root-owned at mode 644. Cursor's hook
' precedence is enterprise > team > project > user, so the sandboxed agent can
' neither edit the file nor out-rank it. That is the whole reason it lives in
' /etc rather than in the agent home.
'
' ── solidity: A VENV INSTEAD OF A PEP 668 OVERRIDE ──────────────────────────
' This layer was `pip3 install --no-cache-dir --break-system-packages semgrep
' solc-select` — 377 MB measured, unpinned, and a PEP 668 override on the SYSTEM
' interpreter that apt also manages, so a later `apt-get install python3-<x>` (or
' an agent doing so at runtime) could produce a broken mixed install. Three fixes
' in one layer: its own prefix (/opt/security), versions that are facts about the
' image, and no shipped bytecode.
'   ARG SEMGREP_VERSION=1.176.1
'   ARG SOLC_SELECT_VERSION=1.2.0
'   ARG SOLHINT_VERSION=6.2.4
'   ARG FOUNDRY_VERSION=v1.8.1
' Only the entry points go on PATH — semgrep, solc-select and solc are symlinked
' into /usr/local/bin. defs/claudecode/tests asserts both `semgrep --version` and
' `solc-select --version`, which is why both are linked.
'
' python3-venv is installed HERE rather than in proveo/claudecode: that image has
' python3 and python3-pip but NOT ensurepip, so `python3 -m venv` fails there
' with "the virtual environment was not created successfully". Only this variant
' needs a venv, so only this variant pays for it.
'
' PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX is set for the same reason as cecli's, one step further on:
' /opt/security is root-owned and the agent is not root, so without a writable
' prefix Python would re-parse every module on every semgrep run.
'
' FOUNDRY WAS INSTALLING NIGHTLIES. `curl -L https://foundry.paradigm.xyz | bash
' && foundryup` takes LATEST when given no argument, and foundry's release feed
' is nightlies with a stable tag every few weeks — so the image's toolchain
' changed under it on every rebuild, which is exactly what
' _spec/_devops/agent-version-pin.puml exists to prevent. `foundryup --install
' <tag>` pins it, and `forge --version` plus `cast --version` make the pin a fact.
'
' foundryup has NO component selector — no flag installs a subset — so anvil and
' chisel are deleted in the SAME RUN. This image audits contracts: forge builds
' and tests them, cast inspects them. anvil is a local devnet and chisel is a
' Solidity REPL, and a sandbox with no chain and no operator at a prompt has use
' for neither. A `rm` in a later RUN would have removed the paths and kept the
' bytes.
'
' THE FOUNDRY PATH ENTRY IS APPENDED, NEVER PREPENDED. `/home/${USER_NAME}` is a
' symlink to /home/agent, which sbx mounts volumes under and the agent can write
' to. At the FRONT of PATH, that directory would let anything written to
' ~/.foundry/bin/<name> shadow the real binary of that name for every later
' command. forge and cast are unique names, so putting them last costs nothing
' and closes the hole.

node "proveo/cecli — FROM proveo/base" as CECLI <<host>> {
  database "``/opt/cecli`` venv\ncecli-dev, ""--no-compile""" as V1 <<db>>
  database "``/opt/serena`` venv\nserena-agent — versions conflict" as V2 <<db>>
  component "``PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX``\n""/tmp/proveo-pycache""" as PYC <<app>>
}

node "proveo/claudecode-solidity" as SOL <<host>> {
  database "``/opt/security`` venv\nsemgrep 1.176.1 · solc-select 1.2.0" as V3 <<db>>
  component "foundry v1.8.1\nforge + cast only" as FOUND <<app>>
}

node "Deliberately absent" as GONE <<host>> {
  component "opencode: ""xclip""\nno DISPLAY, no clipboard to reach" as G1 <<app>>
  component "claudecode: ""typescript ts-node\nprettier eslint"" — 65 MB, unpinned" as G2 <<app>>
  component "claudecode: baked ""NODE_ENV""\nit would skip devDependencies" as G3 <<app>>
  component "cecli: ""build-essential""\none sdist in two closures, pure Python" as G4 <<app>>
}

component "``--break-system-packages``\napt and pip owning one prefix" as PEP <<error>>
component "foundryup with no tag\na nightly toolchain per rebuild" as NIGHTLY <<error>>
component "``~/.foundry/bin`` first on PATH\nan agent-writable dir shadowing binaries" as SHADOW <<error>>
component "``.pyc`` shipped beside ``.py``\n153 MB, then 1850 ms per launch" as BYTES <<error>>
component "HEALTHCHECK hard-codes ``/home/claude``\nany other USER_NAME is never healthy" as HC <<error>>

V1 ARROW_MAIN PYC : written outside a read-only venv
V3 ARROW_MAIN PYC : ""/opt/security"" is root-owned
PYC ARROW_ERROR BYTES : both halves needed —\n""--no-compile"" AND a writable prefix
V3 ARROW_ERROR PEP : replaced it — own prefix,\npinned versions, no bytecode
V2 ARROW_MAIN V2 : its own prefix because\nit conflicts with cecli-dev
FOUND ARROW_ERROR NIGHTLY : ""--install v1.8.1"" +\n""forge --version"" as the proof
FOUND ARROW_ERROR SHADOW : ""ENV PATH=$PATH:…"" — appended
G3 ARROW_ERROR HC : both are claudecode's, and only\none of them is on purpose

note bottom of PYC
  **Neither switch alone is right.**
  pip compiles at INSTALL time, so the runtime
  variable ships the bytes anyway; dropping them
  without a writable prefix pays re-parse forever.
  Doing both is what beat the baseline.
end note

note bottom of V2
  **Pinned because it was deleted once already.**
  An unpinned serena-agent shipped a version skew
  that left the MCP server dead on every boot for
  weeks, and the seed now refuses to declare a
  server that fails the initialize handshake.
end note

note bottom of V3
  **A venv, not a PEP 668 override.**
  Sharing apt's interpreter meant a later
  ""apt-get install python3-<x>"" — or an agent
  doing one at runtime — could produce a broken
  mixed install. Only entry points go on PATH.
end note

note bottom of FOUND
  **No component selector, so delete in the RUN.**
  foundryup installs all four binaries and offers
  no subset flag. anvil is a devnet and chisel a
  REPL; this image audits contracts, and a later
  ""rm"" would keep the bytes.
end note

note bottom of SHADOW
  **Appending is the security decision.**
  ~/.foundry/bin sits under a home sbx mounts and
  the agent can write. First on PATH it shadows
  any binary by name; last it cannot, and forge
  and cast are unique names anyway.
end note

note right of GONE
  **An absence has to be written where it was
  made.** Each of these reads as a missing package
  to the next author, so the image records why the
  clipboard, the compiler, the dev tools and the
  env var were all removed on purpose.
end note

note bottom of HC
  **A build ARG the healthcheck does not read.**
  USER_NAME parameterises the user elsewhere,
  so a build that changes it yields an image that
  is permanently unhealthy. Recorded here rather
  than repaired.
end note

@enduml
